      'Make generation thread-safe within the process. A lock, atomic state transition, or a single generator loop must ensure two threads cannot observe the same timestamp and sequence pair. If the process restarts within the same millisecond under the same worker ID, it may reuse a sequence; preserve last-issued time where needed, wait beyond the prior slot, or lease a new worker identity.',
